---
description: Basic set of rules of engagement
alwaysApply: true
--- 
- Read the CLAUDE.md in the root directory of the project for all the instructions.

- Make your changes simple and short. Oversimplifying is better than overcomplicating.
- If you add code to an existing file, the style of the new code should match the style of the existing code. 
  If you add a new file, its style should match the style of other files in the project.
- Do not commit the code unless explicitly asked to do that.
- When writing commit message, make it short. Write a header line and a 3-4 lines of text explaining the change.